From 2bd32db57eb2264ae369b74ffef74a155e5e8c5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zack <51604064+luoyuctl@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 22:02:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] [Perf][DSv4.1] Warm up small-head sparse decode kernels
 at startup

Route both small-head launches through triton_kernel_dispatcher_with_warmup
and register every split config, HAS_EXTRA variant and DSpark SWA width the
layer can dispatch, so no Triton compile happens on the serving path.

Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: zack <51604064+luoyuctl@users.noreply.github.com>
